WasmCert-Coq v2.0 caps Coq at <8.18, but the formalisation builds unchanged on
8.18, which is the version this project uses. Relax the bound in the two build
metadata files.

Carried as a patch so vendor/WasmCert-Coq stays pinned to canonical upstream
and the trust base is visibly unaffected: nothing here touches a theory file.

diff --git a/coq-wasm.opam b/coq-wasm.opam
index 5a2751d..4a742ce 100644
--- a/coq-wasm.opam
+++ b/coq-wasm.opam
@@ -13,7 +13,7 @@ homepage: "https://github.com/WasmCert/WasmCert-Coq"
 bug-reports: "https://github.com/WasmCert/WasmCert-Coq/issues"
 depends: [
   "dune" {>= "3.0"}
-  "coq" {>= "8.16" & < "8.18~"}
+  "coq" {>= "8.16" & < "8.19~"}
   "coq-compcert" {>= "3.11"}
   "coq-ext-lib" {>= "0.11.8"}
   "coq-mathcomp-ssreflect" {>= "1.16.0" & <= "1.18.0"}
diff --git a/dune-project b/dune-project
index 852c901..6c9ebd7 100644
--- a/dune-project
+++ b/dune-project
@@ -13,7 +13,7 @@
   (synopsis "Wasm formalisation in Coq")
   (description "Wasm formalisation in Coq, following the AFP formalisation of Conrad Watt")
   (depends
-    (coq (and (>= 8.16) (< 8.18~)))
+    (coq (and (>= 8.16) (< 8.19~)))
     (coq-compcert (>= 3.11))
     (coq-ext-lib (>= 0.11.8))
     (coq-mathcomp-ssreflect (and (>= 1.16.0) (<= 1.18.0)))
